{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1157490-complete-newbie-in-rpg","id":1157490,"title":"Complete newbie in Rpg","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-11-10T04:01:39-08:00","id":1157490,"title":"Complete newbie in Rpg","content":"For many many years, I\u2019ve had the project of playing an RPG. Life being what it is, it never happened, for various reasons. However, recently I organised a murder party for my girlfriend and it was a huge success. <br /> <br /> And now she also want to try tabletop rpgs. So, it would, at first, be me as a GM, and her as a character.<br /> <br /> My idea is to do a mystery/horror campaign where she would be an investigator that would uncover supernatural and horrific things over multiple adventures. Eventually she could be attacked by a vampire or a werewolf and become one, or join a group of hunters or something like that. This campaign idea has interested me for a few years now (I have posted about it a while back on rpg net) and I think I found the system which would be best for me to run it.<br /> <br /> I had narrowed it down to three games: Call of Cthulhu, Trail of Cthulhu, and Chronicles of Darkness. I finally rejected Call of cthulhu and trail of cthulhu. I am not a big fan of the cthulhu mythos and I don\u2019t care much for the sanity system in both games. I prefer some traditionnal horror. For ToC, I also thought the system would not work for me. It has good advice on mystery games, but I dislike the ressource management aspect, and the way the clues work. <br /> <br /> Also, CofD is almost exactly what I\u2019m looking for as a setting. However, reading through the book, I found that the rules were a bit too complex for me. So I might ditch some of those rules for now. What rules can be safely ignored, without breaking the system?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21618-super_bruno","name":"super_bruno","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-10T07:01:34-08:00","id":1157523,"title":"","content":"Good for you, I'm playing WoD a while now, GMing for my girlfriend. But first of all, this is the Classic World of Darkness forum, not Chronicles. Look a spot higher in the list. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> That being said, I think it's a lot of fun, doing some 1on1 RP with your girlfriend or really any one person you know well and who's interested. I found, the choice of game system is really important. Now, I mostly played DnD and CWoD games, so that's what I can talk about.<br /> Games like DnD have a really strong emphasis on party and teamwork, being more of a war game with mostly quite the epic stories, while CWoD games put more emphasis on personal development. But I think the latter is also true in CofD. However some of these games might be more fun or easier to gm when there's actually a party of players, not just one.<br /> Personally I think Mage: The Ascension is the perfect game of the Classic World of Darkness to play solo. We want to try Dark Ages: Fey next, but that's also Classic.<br /> <br /> Most important however is that your girlfriend enjoyes the game and the system. Let her have a look and let her choose what she wants to play.<br /> <br /> As for ditching rules... it's hard to get a grip at how important all these rules are, when you just start playing. When I began playing WoD games, we started very slowly, discussed how different rules would work out and could influence the game. Willpower points being a major factor, as you can play willpower heavy or let characters starve for willpower, making them quite valuable. Talk with your girlfriend how she would like the game to be and adapt. There's nothing stopping you from establishing a few houserules in your very first chronicle to help you get started and make things simpler.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13221-thevarulfen","name":"TheVarulfen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-10T07:17:08-08:00","id":1157524,"title":"","content":"Both Mage: The Ascension and Vampire: The Masquerade (or Dark Ages) are very good for 1 Player 1 ST games. Vampire may be the easier of the two for the first time out but Mage does have a free quick start on DriveThruRPG.com","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-07T17:05:21-08:00","id":1165977,"title":"","content":"I suggest trying to run as close to RAW (rules as written) as possible for the first session or two. This lets you see what works for you and what doesn't. You also don't have to use every system in every session. This is especially true of the different conflict resolution systems. Plan one session to try the combat system, one to try the investigation system, one to try the social manipulation system and one to try the chase system (or try two systems per session if that works better for you). <br /> <br /> Discuss how it went after the game and then decide if it works for you as is or not, if you would like too change it and how or if you want to axe it all together. Also, most of those systems can be replaced with a roll or two, even combat has a one or two roll variant in CoD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23589,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23589-jimalcoatl","user":"Jimalcoatl","date":". 12-07-2017, 08:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23589-jimalcoatl","name":"Jimalcoatl","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}